        "kind": "requirement",
        "meaning": "If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee, including employees who are exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act's (FLSA) recordkeeping requirement (such as bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees as defined in FLSA Regulations, 29 CFR part 541), the employer bears the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours."
